    "q-66546": {
      "dom_id": "step-q66546",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "What exponential equation is equivalent to the logarithmic equation $\\operatorname{log}⁡a=\\frac{1}{2}?$",
      "worked_solution": "The common logarithm of $a$ is defined as follows:\n\n$\\operatorname{log}⁡a=x$ is equivalent to $a={10}^{x}$\n\nIf we compare $\\operatorname{log}⁡a=\\frac{1}{2}$ with $\\operatorname{log}⁡a=x,$ we get that $x=\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the given equation can be expressed as ${10}^{1/2}=a.$\n\nFinally, since ${10}^{1/2}=\\sqrt{10},$ the equation $\\operatorname{log}⁡a=\\frac{1}{2}$ is equivalent to $\\sqrt{10}=a.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
