    "q-108087": {
      "dom_id": "step-q108087",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Find the value of $2\\operatorname{log}⁡({t}^{3})-\\operatorname{log}⁡(10t)$ at $t=10.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we substitute $t=10$ into the function. This gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{log}⁡({t}^{3})-\\operatorname{log}⁡(10t) & =2\\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{3})-\\operatorname{log}⁡(10\\cdot 10) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{3})-\\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe common logarithm reverses the action of the exponent. The principle is:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{x})=x\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $x=3$ and $x=2.$ Therefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{3})-\\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{2})=2\\cdot 3-2=4\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
