    "q-24882": {
      "dom_id": "step-q24882",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Find the value of $\\operatorname{log}⁡({t}^{2})+\\operatorname{log}⁡(10t)$ at $t=10.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we substitute $t=10$ into the function. This gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{log}⁡({t}^{2})+\\operatorname{log}⁡(10t) & =\\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{2})+\\operatorname{log}⁡(10\\cdot 10) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{2})+\\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe common logarithm reverses the action of the exponent. The principle is:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{x})=x\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $x=2.$ Therefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{2})+\\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{2})=2+2=4\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
