    "q-66630": {
      "dom_id": "step-q66630",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "$\\operatorname{log}⁡(\\sqrt[3]{10})=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we rewrite $\\sqrt[{}^{3}]{10}$ as a power of $10$ (the base of the common logarithm) as follows:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[3]{10}={10}^{1/3}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{log}⁡(\\sqrt[3]{10})=\\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{1/3})\n$$\n\nThe common logarithm reverses the action of the exponent. The principle is:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{x})=x\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $x=\\frac{1}{3}.$ Therefore:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{1/3})=\\frac{1}{3}\n$$",
