      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "Rounded to $3$ decimal places, $\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(8)}{3\\operatorname{log}⁡(11)}=$",
      "worked_solution": "We compute the required expression to $3$ decimal places using a calculator, rounding the intermediate steps to $6$ decimal places to avoid rounding error. This gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(8)}{3\\operatorname{log}⁡(11)} & ≈\\frac{0.903\\,090}{3(1.041\\,393)} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.903\\,090}{3.124\\,179} \\\\  & ≈0.289\\,065 \\\\  & ≈0.289\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
