    "q-78745": {
      "dom_id": "step-q78745",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "Rounded to $3$ decimal places, find the value of $f(x)=3\\operatorname{log}⁡(2x)-2\\operatorname{log}⁡(5x)$ at $x=3.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we replace $x=3$ and get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(3) & =3\\operatorname{log}⁡(2\\cdot 3)-2\\operatorname{log}⁡(5\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{log}⁡(6)-2\\operatorname{log}⁡(15)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe compute the required value to $3$ decimal places using a calculator, rounding the intermediate steps to $6$ decimal places to avoid rounding error. This gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(3) & =3\\operatorname{log}⁡(6)-2\\operatorname{log}⁡(15) \\\\  & ≈3(0.778\\,151)-2(1.176\\,091) \\\\  & =2.334\\,453-2.352\\,182 \\\\  & =-0.017\\,729 \\\\  & ≈-0.018\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
